This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up the flame sensor and temperature sensor, and sets up the buzzer. It then enters a main loop that reads the flame sensor and temperature sensor, and checks for flame and temperature. If both are detected, it logs the event and sounds the buzzer for 2 seconds. If only the flame sensor is detected, it logs "Flame detected!". If only the temperature sensor is detected, it logs the temperature reading. If the ADC read fails, it logs an error and continues without crashing. The code also handles SIGINT by setting a running flag to 0 so the main loop exits cleanly, then turning off the buzzer, deregistering the ISR, closing the I2C handle, closing the log file, and calling gpioTerminate().

