The code also implements robust error handling by checking every I2C syscall (open, ioctl, write, read) and handling sensor-absent or bus-error paths by logging the error and retrying after 5 seconds. It ensures clean resource release on all exit paths by closing the I2C file descriptor and the CSV log file, and uses signal handling (SIGINT, SIGTERM) for graceful shutdown.

The code logs timestamped readings to a comma-separated environmental_data.csv file and displays the data on the console for real-time monitoring in a weather station prototype. It samples every 5 seconds.

