This code uses the `pigpio` library to control the GPIO pins and the `mcp3008` library to read the analog input from the Vegetronix VH400 sensor. It also uses the `signal` library to handle the `SIGINT` signal, which is sent when the user presses `Ctrl+C` to terminate the program.

The `spi_init`, `adc_init`, and `pump_init` functions are used to initialize the SPI, ADC, and GPIO interfaces, respectively. The `read_adc` function reads the analog input from the sensor and returns the value as an integer. The `log_event` function writes a message to the log file with a timestamp.

The `sigint_handler` function is called when the `SIGINT` signal is received. It turns off the pump and closes the GPIO and ADC interfaces before exiting the program.

The main loop reads the analog input from the sensor and checks if it is below the threshold. If it is, it turns on the pump and logs a message. It then sleeps for the watering duration and turns off the pump. It then sleeps for the watering interval before repeating the process.

Note that this code assumes that the Vegetronix VH400 sensor is connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W via the SPI interface, and that the 12V submersible water pump is connected to GPIO18. You may need to modify the code to match your specific hardware configuration.

