This code uses the `spidev` library to communicate with the MCP3008 ADC over SPI. It sets the SPI mode, bits, and speed, and then sends a 3-byte command to the ADC to read channel 0. It then reads the 3-byte response and extracts the 10-bit raw value from it. Finally, it calculates the voltage and prints it to the console. The code handles errors and closes the SPI device file descriptor on all exit paths.

