This code opens the camera device at `/dev/video0`, checks if it is a V4L2 video capture device, negotiates format 640x480, V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV, V4L2_FIELD_NONE, and uses memory-mapped streaming with one buffer. It then starts streaming, waits for the frame, dequeues the buffer, verifies the captured width, height, and pixel format match the requested values, crops the region starting at (100, 50) with size 200x150 from the YUYV frame, and saves the cropped frame to `cropped.yuv`. Finally, it cleans up by munmapping the buffer, closing the file descriptor, and freeing the memory.

