This code uses the pigpio library to read pulses from the YF-S201 water flow sensor connected to GPIO17, calculates the flow rate in liters per minute using the sensor's calibration figure of approximately 450 pulses per liter, and logs the current flow rate and the running total volume to the console every 1 second. It also updates a small HD44780 LCD screen connected via I2C (bus 1, address 0x27) to display the current flow rate together with the accumulated volume every 10 seconds. The code handles GPIO initialization failures, I2C communication errors, and SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for a graceful shutdown that releases all GPIO and I2C resources.

