This code uses the `pigpio` library to interface with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and I2C peripherals, and the `i2c` library to communicate with the TDK InvenSense CH201 ultrasonic Time-of-Flight sensor over I2C bus 1. The code sets up the I2C bus and GPIO pins, and then enters a loop that reads the distance from the sensor, maps the distance to a blink frequency, and blinks an LED on GPIO 18 at that frequency. The code also sets up SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers to clean up and exit gracefully when the program is interrupted.

