This code uses the `pigpio` library to interface with the VL53L1X sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x29. It configures the sensor for continuous ranging mode and reads distance measurements every 500 ms. If the measured distance is below 100 mm, it activates an active buzzer connected to GPIO 22. The code handles I2C errors gracefully by logging the error and skipping the iteration. It ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including handling SIGINT for graceful shutdown. The continuous ranging configuration is applied exactly once at startup and re-applied automatically if a re-initialization is required after an I2C error. The buzzer is switched off again as soon as the measured distance rises back above the 100 mm threshold.

