The main loop reads ambient light data from registers 0x22-0x23 and proximity data from registers 0x24-0x25, each as a 16-bit little-endian value. It converts the ambient light data to lux using the formula `lux = raw * 0.1`, and logs the timestamped reading to `biometric_log.txt` in CSV format as `timestamp,lux,proximity`. It also prints the same reading to stdout.

The code sets up SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers to close the I2C device and log file on receipt of these signals. It also checks every I2C read/write operation for errors and handles sensor absence (a failed part ID read) gracefully by printing an error message and exiting the program.

Note that this code assumes that the I2C bus is already enabled and that the Si1182-A-GM sensor is connected to the I2C bus at address 0x39. If this is not the case, you may need to modify the code to match your specific hardware configuration.

