```
This code uses the pigpio library to interface with the Sensirion SCD40 CO2 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x62. It starts the periodic measurement mode, reads the data ready status, and reads the measurement data if the data ready status is set. It then validates the CRC-8 checksum for each data word and stores the data in a circular buffer. It also turns on an LED on GPIO17 when the CO2 concentration exceeds 1000 ppm. The code handles sensor-absent or bus-error paths by printing an error message and exiting the program. It also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to gracefully shut down the sensor, close the I2C handle, release the GPIO, and terminate pigpio.

