This code uses the `libgpiod` library to read the value of the GPIO line connected to the flame sensor every 100 milliseconds. If the flame is detected, the current time is obtained using `clock_gettime` and the flame detection is logged to a file using `fprintf`. The code also handles errors and cleans up resources on all exit paths using `gpiod_line_close`, `gpiod_chip_close`, and `fclose`.

