This code uses the `pigpio` library to read the GPIO pin connected to the SEN0193 Water Level Sensor. It initializes the GPIO pin and reads its value every 2 seconds. If the value is 1, it prints an alert message to `stdout` and appends a timestamped entry to `flood_log.txt`. If the GPIO read fails, it attempts to reinitialize the GPIO pin after 60 seconds. The code also handles `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals to clean up and exit gracefully.

