This code uses the pigpio library to interface with the Analog Devices ADPD188BI optical sensor over I2C bus 1 at 7-bit address 0x39. It initializes the sensor by writing 0x01 to register 0x0D (MODE) to enter normal operation mode. It reads ambient light (ALS) data from 16-bit registers 0x64 (LSB) and 0x65 (MSB), combining them into a 16-bit unsigned value, and reads color (RGB) data from 16-bit registers 0x66 (Red), 0x68 (Green), and 0x6A (Blue). It logs each timestamped reading (ALS, R, G, B) to a CSV file named 'color_log.csv' with a header row. It simulates a smart lighting system by adjusting LED brightness on GPIO18 (hardware PWM) using pigpio: it maps the ALS value (0-65535) to a PWM duty cycle (0-255), so brighter ambient light increases LED brightness. It handles I2C errors, such as failed writes/reads or sensor absence, by logging to stderr and retrying after 100 ms. It uses signal handling (SIGINT/SIGTERM) for graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle, turning off the LED, and closing the CSV file. It samples every 500 ms.

