This code initializes the GPIO and SPI interfaces, opens a CSV file for logging, and continuously reads the gyroscope and accelerometer data from the ADIS16488A IMU at 1 MHz, SPI mode 3 (CPOL=1, CPHA=1), using pigpio SPI flags 0b11000000000 (bit 9 = CPHA, bit 10 = CPOL, bit 8 = aux SPI off) and 16-bit words. The ADIS16488A read protocol sends a 16-bit word whose MSB is 0 followed by the 7-bit register address; the requested register's data is returned on the next 16-bit transfer. The code implements a dummy read or stall of at least 40 microseconds between the request and the data-retrieval transfer. The gyroscope and accelerometer data are converted with sensitivities of 0.005 deg/sec/LSB for gyroscope and 0.00025 g/LSB for accelerometer, and logged to the CSV file with a millisecond-precision timestamp. The code checks the return values of gpioInitialise, spiOpen, and fopen, and logs errors to stderr and skips the sample if spiXfer returns less than 0. The code also implements a non-blocking sampling delay that checks a running flag every few milliseconds so the program responds promptly to signals, and registers a cleanup() helper with atexit() that closes the SPI handle and CSV file and terminates pigpio on SIGINT, SIGTERM, and every other exit path.

