This code uses the standard Linux /dev/i2c-1 ioctl interface to communicate with the BH1750FVI light sensor over I2C bus 1 (GPIO2/GPIO3). It sets the I2C slave address to 0x23, which is the default address for the sensor when the ADDR pin is tied to GND. It then sets the One-Time High-Resolution Mode 2 command using the I2C_WRITE_CMD constant, and waits for the maximum conversion time of 180 ms. After the conversion is complete, it reads 2 bytes of data from the sensor and calculates the illuminance in lux using the formula (raw_value * 5) / 6. The calculated lux value is then logged to a file named 'light_log.txt', along with a timestamp. The program handles potential I2C write/read errors and sensor-absent paths by checking the return values of the ioctl and read functions, and by closing the I2C bus and log file on all exit paths. It also implements clean resource release by using the close function to close the I2C bus and log file, and by using the fclose function to close the log file.

