This code uses the pigpio library to control the door lock with a servo motor on GPIO18 (PWM-capable) and two push buttons, a lock button on GPIO21 and an unlock button on GPIO22, each using an external or internal pull-up so that pressing reads as active-low (0). When the lock button is pressed, the servo moves to the locked position with a pulse width of 1000 microseconds (about 0 degrees); when the unlock button is pressed, the servo moves to the unlocked position with a pulse width of 2000 microseconds (about 180 degrees). The code also debounces each button press with a 100 ms delay and constrains the servo pulse width to the safe range of 500-2500 microseconds at all times. The code handles initialization failures gracefully, prints status messages, uses only pigpio API calls, and cleans up all resources on exit through a SIGINT signal handler.

