This code uses the pigpio library to decode NEC IR remote signals from an IR receiver such as a TSOP38238 connected to GPIO17 (BCM). It registers a pigpio alert callback on the falling edge to capture pulse timings, and decodes the 32-bit NEC frame using its 9 ms mark plus 4.5 ms space header, 560 microsecond bit marks, 1690 microsecond spaces for logic 1, and 560 microsecond spaces for logic 0. The decoded address and command are validated against their inverted copies, and logged to syslog. The decoded commands are also published to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 on topic ir/decoded, using paho-mqtt v2 callback semantics. The code checks pigpio initialization, handles GPIO initialization failures, guards against pulse buffer overflow, validates the NEC checksum, and cleans up pigpio, MQTT, and syslog resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

